WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.920
The superhero life isn't cheap — luckily,&nbsp;
many of Marvel's most powerful heroes have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:12.240
plenty of cash to burn. From literal gods with&nbsp;
untold fortunes to billionaire investors and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.400
landed aristocrats, these are the&nbsp;
richest heroes in the Marvel universe.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.600
Joey Chapman is the latest in a long&nbsp;
line of English heroes who have fought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.120
evil as Union Jack. While the previous Union&nbsp;
Jacks were part of the wealthy Falsworth family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.640
Chapman was born into the working class, and&nbsp;
earned his mask through a baptism by fire.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.160
Chapman's entry into the Falsworth&nbsp;
family comes through his best friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.920
Kenneth Crichton . Crichton is the&nbsp;
grandson of Lord Brian Falsworth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.960
who fought alongside the team known as “The&nbsp;
Invaders” in World War II. Shortly after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.560
Crichton reveals this to Chapman, the vampire&nbsp;
Baron Blood infiltrates the Falsworth mansion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.960
Chapman dons the costume and proves his&nbsp;
worth in battle against the vampire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.680
leading Kenneth to suggest that it should be&nbsp;
Chapman who carries on the Union Jack tradition.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.160
Despite his humble beginnings, Chapman's&nbsp;
access to the Falsworth fortune and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.400
own work with the British Secret Service&nbsp;
affords him plenty of resources to pursue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.880
his fight against evil. This wealth&nbsp;
helps pay for his numerous gadgets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.800
his bulletproof costume, and&nbsp;
Beryl, his high-tech motorcycle.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.200
Stephen Strange begins his&nbsp;
superheroic journey by spending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.280
all the wealth he earned as a surgeon&nbsp;
on anything that might heal his hands.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.320
"3D printing a scaffold — if I could get a loan&nbsp;
together, just a small loan…" "Stephen, you've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.080
always spent money as fast as you can make it, but&nbsp;
now you're spending money you don't even have."

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.680
Becoming a master of the mystic arts eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.520
mends his broken digits — and&nbsp;
it makes him rich again, too.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.800
Doctor Strange's wealth is made most clear in&nbsp;
the ownership and upkeep of his Greenwich Village&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:52.560
Sanctum Sanctorum , and the long employment of&nbsp;
his faithful friend and comrade in arms, Wong.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.120
There are plenty of other obvious examples&nbsp;
of his wealth lying around his home, too:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:02.320
While many of the antiques and artifacts in&nbsp;
his vast collection are no doubt the product&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.760
of adventure, some of them were just&nbsp;
as likely purchased by Strange himself.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:13.920
Moreover, in 1989's Doctor Strange, Sorcerer&nbsp;
Supreme #11, readers learn Strange owns a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:19.520
nearby warehouse, for the sole purpose of storing&nbsp;
the cryogenically frozen corpse of his brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.080
Victor. Earlier in that series, Strange's&nbsp;
pockets prove deep enough for his friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:29.040
Sara Wolfe to set up a memorial foundation in&nbsp;
his name, after he is believed to have died.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.640
As any fan of Highlander will&nbsp;
know, living for many centuries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:41.680
is a sure-fire way to get rich. This is a lesson&nbsp;
well-learned by the eons-old Ulysses Bloodstone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.080
a caveman saddled with a mystical&nbsp;
stone that gives him both his surname&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:52.480
and his unnaturally long life. Ulysses spends his&nbsp;
considerable time on Earth hunting monsters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.040
searching for Ulluxy'l Kwan Tae Syn , the&nbsp;
creature who destroyed his ancient tribe.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:02.080
Ulysses eventually finds both vengeance&nbsp;
and his long-awaited eternal reward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:08.800
but not before siring a daughter. In 2001's&nbsp;
Bloodstone #1, Marvel introduced Elsa Bloodstone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.880
who learns of her father's fantastic&nbsp;
past while settling his estate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.800
Not long after, with the help of&nbsp;
the fabled gem her father left her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.280
and a solid set of superpowers, Elsa&nbsp;
follows in her father's footsteps.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:26.400
Elsa also inherited Ulysses' massive&nbsp;
fortune upon his death. Her first solo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.440
series was short lived, but she continues to&nbsp;
use her wealth to fund her crusade against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:37.600
the world's monsters — perhaps most memorably in&nbsp;
the acclaimed series, Nextwave: Agents of H.A.T.E.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:43.920
Janet Van Dyne, better known as the Wasp, begins&nbsp;
her crime-fighting career after the death of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.760
her father, Vernon. Vernon was a world-renowned&nbsp;
inventor at the time of his death, and his demise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:55.920
not only inspires Janet to become a hero, but&nbsp;
also gifts her with a ton of cash. And she's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.280
shy about it, either — early on in her Avenging&nbsp;
days, Janet is known both among her teammates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:06.720
and the public as a socialite and an incorrigible&nbsp;
flirt, not to mention a fashion plate.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:13.040
And although she later curbs her more extravagant&nbsp;
impulses, Janet never entirely loses her love of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:18.160
the finer things in life. A fashion designer&nbsp;
whose career predates her time as an Avenger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:23.200
Janet uses her fortune to further her&nbsp;
art. She changes her costume so often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:29.280
that it's not at all rare to see her in one outfit&nbsp;
in one issue, and a different one in the next. Her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.920
designs can also be glimpsed in other corners&nbsp;
of the Marvel universe: for example, Karolina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:38.880
Dean can be spotted wearing Van Dyne-branded&nbsp;
clothing in the 2017 Runaways comic series.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:45.440
Often, when new writers and artists are assigned&nbsp;
superheroes who have never been particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:50.640
popular, those creators like to shake up the&nbsp;
character's essential traits. Marc Spector,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:56.240
AKA Moon Knight, is a perfect example of&nbsp;
this, as recent takes on the character have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:02.480
tended to minimize the fact that this mentally&nbsp;
splintered superhero is a bonafide billionaire.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:08.560
Long before he became the Fist of Khonshu, Spector&nbsp;
was a renowned mercenary and heavyweight boxing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:13.760
champion. By the time he begins fighting evil as&nbsp;
Moon Knight, his investments have yielded some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:19.600
serious rewards. While his resources are not&nbsp;
inherited as Bruce Wayne's are, Spector's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:25.520
wealth is one of the reasons some fans see him as&nbsp;
Marvel's answer to Batman. Not only does he mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:31.520
work at night, but his wealth also affords him&nbsp;
an arsenal of themed weapons, vehicles, gadgets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:37.520
and costumes. And sure, he's not as widely known&nbsp;
in the Marvel universe as Batman is within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:43.760
world of DC Comics, but Moon Knight isn't to be&nbsp;
underestimated. Dude has a Moon-copter, after all.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:51.840
"Honestly, Charles. I don't know how&nbsp;
you survived… living in such hardship."]

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:55.760
Little of the good Charles&nbsp;
Xavier has done for mutant-kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.440
would have been possible without&nbsp;
his considerable wealth. Indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:04.720
the grounds and the mansion used for Xavier's&nbsp;
School for Gifted Youngsters is inherited from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:10.080
his father. That fortune was likewise used to&nbsp;
build the more secret areas of Xavier's School,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.120
such as the Danger Room, in addition to the&nbsp;
X-Men's vast variety of high-tech vehicles.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.440
Thanks to a story from the early&nbsp;
'00s, we know that at that time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:26.160
Charles Xavier's net worth was $3.5&nbsp;
billion. This is revealed in 2002's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:33.120
New X-Men #129, when the artificially-evolved&nbsp;
mutant known as Fantomex tries to extort Xavier.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:38.880
Of course, it's likely that Xavier's fortune&nbsp;
has increased considerably since 2002.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:44.480
Not only is the founder of the X-Men known for&nbsp;
investing wisely, but the 2019 event Dawn of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:50.720
X likely did a lot of good for Xavier's bottom&nbsp;
line. In this arc, Xavier helps to found a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.600
sovereign mutant state on the sentient mutant&nbsp;
island of Krakoa , a process that includes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:01.240
brokering lucrative deals with other nations who&nbsp;
are seeking medicines only available on Krakoa.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:06.880
Warren Worthington III has often acted&nbsp;
as one of the X-Men's deepest pockets:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.000
Having inherited billions from his family as&nbsp;
well as ownership of Worthington industries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.880
Archangel funds everything from missions&nbsp;
to equipment. In fact, it has not been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.520
unheard of for Charles Xavier himself to borrow&nbsp;
money from Archangel in order to make repairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.480
additions, and improvements&nbsp;
to his Westchester school.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:29.680
Financially speaking, Warren is also solely&nbsp;
responsible for the founding of the first version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:35.040
of X-Factor, the team set up by the original&nbsp;
X-Men to hunt and secretly help mutants on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:40.560
run. It's Warren who bankrolls their equipment,&nbsp;
their headquarters, and their new uniforms.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.160
Warren's history has often worked&nbsp;
against his resources, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:49.040
such as when his board of directors uses his&nbsp;
temporary amnesia to take the company from him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:54.480
Thankfully, in 2012's Wolverine and the&nbsp;
X-Men #19, Warren successfully takes back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.720
his family's company — with a little help&nbsp;
from ace attorney Matt Murdock, of course.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:06.000
Daniel Rand is more than just a master of kung&nbsp;
fu and the hard-won wielder of the Iron Fist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.480
He's also CEO of the Rand Corporation,&nbsp;
a position which has afforded Rand and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:16.800
his allies many comforts and advantages. But&nbsp;
it has also attracted plenty of new enemies.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.600
Originally the Rand-Meachum Corporation, the&nbsp;
company passes briefly into the care of Harold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.480
Meachum, Daniel's father's old business partner.&nbsp;
Wendell Rand had visited the mystical city of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:31.680
K'un-Lun once upon a time, and searches for it&nbsp;
in the snows of Tibet years later, with his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:37.120
wife, and Meachum in tow. Disaster strikes,&nbsp;
however, and when Wendell hangs helplessly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:42.000
from the edge of a precipice, Meachum turns&nbsp;
on him and throws him to his death. Daniel's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.480
mother Heather subsequently sacrifices&nbsp;
herself to save Daniel from hungry wolves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:51.120
allowing the young Danny Rand to find&nbsp;
shelter — and more — in K'un-Lun.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:55.920
As an adult, Danny returns to&nbsp;
NYC and regains control of Rand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:59.760
though his revenge on Meachum is&nbsp;
stolen from him by an assassin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:05.840
He has since used his vast wealth to fund his&nbsp;
work as the immortal Iron Fist, including funding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:11.160
the Heroes for Hire, an organization Rand&nbsp;
and Luke Cage founded to help fight crime.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:18.400
Kyle Richmond, AKA Nighthawk, is perhaps the&nbsp;
most obscure of Marvel's wealthy heroes. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:22.320
part of the Squadron Sinister, he&nbsp;
was originally a villainous Batman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:27.120
clone in a group of villains blatantly&nbsp;
modeled after DC Comics' Justice League.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:32.480
He later changes sides, most prominently as&nbsp;
a regular in Marvel's first Defenders series.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:37.280
Like many rich Marvel heroes, Kyle Richmond&nbsp;
inherited his wealth from his father — in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:42.240
this case Arthur Richmond, owner of Richmond&nbsp;
Enterprises. Nighthawk doesn't always prove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:46.800
to be a vigilant owner of the company he&nbsp;
inherited, however. While he's busy first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:52.080
committing crime and then fighting it, he allows&nbsp;
his friend J.C. Pennysworth to handle the reins.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:55.840
Pennysworth is later revealed to be&nbsp;
the head of the racist terror group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:01.840
the Sons of the Serpent, which makes you wonder if&nbsp;
Nighthawk really did his due diligence on the guy.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:07.040
Richmond subsequently uses his wealth to establish&nbsp;
the Richmond Riding Academy, which doubles as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:13.200
base of operations for the Defenders. Or at least,&nbsp;
it's intended to serve as such. With team members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:18.640
Hulk and Doctor Strange often not showing up for&nbsp;
work, Richmond complains about all the money he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:24.080
spent for nothing — particularly on the oversized&nbsp;
conference chair he had made for the Hulk.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:31.200
While Professor X's history is not without its&nbsp;
moral ambiguity, Marvel Comics canon has long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:35.760
maintained that he never uses his psychic&nbsp;
abilities to help with his investments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:42.480
However, Xavier isn't Marvel's only psychic, and&nbsp;
they don't all share his principles. Emma Frost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:47.520
certainly isn't afraid to use her formidable&nbsp;
telepathy to gain an edge in the financial world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:53.520
It's likely a good chunk of her wealth may come&nbsp;
from even sketchier ventures. Frost is, after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:58.960
the former White Queen of the Hellfire Club,&nbsp;
which is not known for its respect of the law.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:04.000
Emma is the heiress to the Frost fortune,&nbsp;
including Frost International, which specializes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:09.760
in technology and electronics. When the X-Men&nbsp;
establish the mutant safe haven of Utopia, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:15.920
Frost's wealth alone that supports the island. Her&nbsp;
power has grown considerably in recent years, too:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:20.240
With almost the entire population of Earth's&nbsp;
mutants having joined the sovereign nation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:25.520
Krakoa, Frost's position on the island's&nbsp;
Quiet Council is a lofty perch indeed.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:32.240
Reed Richards isn't exactly obsessed with hoarding&nbsp;
wealth; Put him in a lab and give him the chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:37.840
to explore the cosmos, and you've got a happy&nbsp;
Mr. Fantastic. But believe it or not, the upkeep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:43.600
of an active portal to the Negative Zone and the&nbsp;
storage space for a fleet of Fantasti-Cars isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:48.480
cheap. So it's a good thing Richards also&nbsp;
happens to be one of Marvel's wealthiest heroes.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:52.720
Richards wasn't always wealthy, but the&nbsp;
patents for the inventions he churns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:58.240
not to mention the merchandising rights for the&nbsp;
Fantastic Four, bring in the big bucks. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:02.000
Reed is the kind of guy who doesn't&nbsp;
see his riches until they're gone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:07.040
Thus, he and the rest of the Fantastic Four&nbsp;
are hit hard when their property is seized in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:12.320
an early 2000s storyline. After Doctor Doom&nbsp;
is dragged to Hell, the team dismantles the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:17.360
government of Latveria in the hopes of undoing&nbsp;
Doom's years of tyranny. When they return home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:21.600
their assets are seized by the government&nbsp;
because of their unsanctioned invasion of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:26.400
foreign nation. It isn't until Richards emerges&nbsp;
as one of the most prominent pro-government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:30.880
heroes in Civil War that the United States&nbsp;
releases their stranglehold on his property.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:38.080
Unlike many of the richest Marvel heroes, Sable&nbsp;
didn't inherit anything from her family — unless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:42.400
you count the skills she's used to become one&nbsp;
of the world's most well-known mercenaries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.240
Her father trained her to fight after&nbsp;
the murder of her mother, and Sable went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:50.720
on to found her own soldier-for-hire&nbsp;
company, Silver Sable International.

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:55.200
Silver Sable's wealth is enough to afford&nbsp;
her the acquisition of high-tech weaponry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.200 --> 00:13:00.720
and a vast variety of other equipment made&nbsp;
from cutting edge materials. It is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:05.760
enough to allow her to hire other world-class&nbsp;
mercenaries, including super-powered operatives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:10.640
Although she can be cutthroat in business,&nbsp;
Sable doesn't amass her riches for riches'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:15.560
sake. Much of her wealth goes to aid her&nbsp;
homeland, the fictional nation of Symkaria.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:21.600
Like Thor, the Marvel hero Hercules isn't&nbsp;
just a modern-day strongman with a love of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:28.640
Greco-Roman myth — he's the genuine god, and his&nbsp;
long life has afforded him some very deep pockets.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:34.400
This is never more clear than upon the news of&nbsp;
his temporary death in 2010's Hercules: Fall of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:40.480
Avenger #1. When Venus and Namora do the hard work&nbsp;
of closing out Hercules' estate, they learn he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:46.640
one of the first investors in Stark Industries. He&nbsp;
initially invested $100,000 in the young company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:52.400
and at the time of the strongman's death, that&nbsp;
investment was worth, quote, "a second line of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:58.320
zeroes." He also owns a large number of breweries&nbsp;
and wineries, as well as apartments and homes all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:03.200
across the globe. And while Hercules is one&nbsp;
of the richest heroes in Marvel, it seems that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:08.720
he himself may not even know it, as Venus and&nbsp;
Namora discover that he apparently forgot about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:14.880
most of his investments. If ever there were a&nbsp;
superhero in need of an accountant, it's this guy.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:16.960
"Big man in a suit of armour.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:22.320
Take that off, what are you?" "Genius,&nbsp;
billionaire, playboy philanthropist."

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:28.240
When you think of rich Marvel heroes, it's a sure&nbsp;
bet that you'll probably think of Tony Stark.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:32.800
He may have inherited his huge fortune and&nbsp;
Stark Industries from his father Howard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.920
but Stark can't be accused&nbsp;
of sitting on his laurels.

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:41.120
In fact, it's likely that no single person has&nbsp;
more to do with the upkeep of the Avengers than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:46.800
Tony Stark. More often than not, his wealth&nbsp;
has financed the team, even before he reveals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:52.320
his secret identity to his colleagues and, later,&nbsp;
the public at large. It's Stark who owns Avengers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:57.360
Mansion, it's Stark who employs their butler,&nbsp;
Edwin Jarvis, and it's Stark who pays for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:02.960
and designs the team's Quinjets. Not to mention,&nbsp;
of course, the considerable amount of time, money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:07.440
and resources Stark puts toward designing&nbsp;
and building his many Iron Man suits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:12.560
nor the innovations he's created for other heroes,&nbsp;
such as Spider-Man's famous Iron Spider suit.

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:19.840
There are characters whose wealth is almost&nbsp;
impossible to quantify, because their existence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:25.360
is utterly incomparable to anything&nbsp;
in the real world. Black Bolt, Medusa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:30.720
and the rest of the Inhuman royal family are&nbsp;
a perfect example of this. The Inhumans are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:36.480
a subspecies of humanity that was experimented&nbsp;
upon by the alien Kree millennia ago, a process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:42.160
that granted them extraordinary abilities…&nbsp;
and access to stunning amounts of wealth.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:46.160
Having made homes in both the Himalayas&nbsp;
and on the Blue Area of the Moon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:51.440
the royal family claims real estate holdings&nbsp;
that are entirely priceless. They also have in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:56.160
their possession advanced Kree technology,&nbsp;
which plenty of Earth's militaries would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.160 --> 00:16:00.800
pay dearly to get their hands on. Finally,&nbsp;
the family possesses the Terrigen Crystals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:04.480
which are counted among the rarest&nbsp;
materials in the Solar System.

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:11.120
Namor , the King of Atlantis claims all of the&nbsp;
Earth's oceans as his kingdom, and — according&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:15.920
to him — the ships that traverse them are&nbsp;
allowed to do so only because of his charity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:18.960
While few world leaders recognize Namor's claim to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:23.760
two-thirds of the Earth's surface, he&nbsp;
certainly has the muscle to back it up.

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:28.640
When you're a superpowered world-ruler in&nbsp;
Marvel Comics, losing your throne becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.640 --> 00:16:34.560
kind of a big deal. As such, Namor has found&nbsp;
himself dethroned more times than anyone can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:40.320
count. Yet even without a kingdom, the Sub-Mariner&nbsp;
has managed to secure significant wealth for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:46.000
himself. Early in the '90s Namor the Sub-Mariner&nbsp;
series, for example, Namor reinvents himself as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:51.680
a businessman by using various treasures from the&nbsp;
deep. The fortune these rarities bring him allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:56.400
him to found Oracle Inc., with the intention&nbsp;
of using its wealth to heal the environment.

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:03.600
No organization on Earth could surpass Wakanda&nbsp;
in terms of net worth, and no individual could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:09.040
top T'Challa , the king of Wakanda and the&nbsp;
superhero known as Black Panther. Though the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:14.960
2016 Black Panther series sees T'Challa's power as&nbsp;
ruler rendered less absolute by a new democratic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:19.920
government, he still has more control over his&nbsp;
nation's wealth than any other single person.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:24.240
The source of the nation's wealth is&nbsp;
vibranium , a substance that cannot be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:29.120
found in significant amounts anywhere&nbsp;
else on Earth. Vibranium is the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.440
versatile metal on Earth, and has helped&nbsp;
to make Wakanda not only the richest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:36.960
but also the most technologically&nbsp;
advanced nation on the planet.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:40.240
While T'Challa doesn't often&nbsp;
flex his financial muscles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:45.200
it's not unheard of, either. For example, in&nbsp;
the 2002 Black Panther storyline "Enemy of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:49.280
State II," in which he finds himself&nbsp;
at cross purposes with Tony Stark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:55.360
T'Challa stages a hostile takeover of Stark&nbsp;
Enterprises — with seemingly no effort at all.

00:17:56.560 --> 00:18:00.720
There are some riches whose worth&nbsp;
cannot be properly counted with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:05.120
numbers — and many of them are the&nbsp;
property of Thor, the god of thunder.

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:09.760
"Slow down, there's a few people in the room&nbsp;
who don't understand. Not me, I get it."

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:16.480
In 2019's Thor #16, Odin steps aside,&nbsp;
allowing Thor to become the new All-Father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:22.160
and the king of Asgard. Once that happens, every&nbsp;
drop of gold in the land in the golden realm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:28.400
becomes the property of the mighty Thor — as well&nbsp;
as all the artifacts locked away in Odin's vaults.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:33.920
One of the most valuable artifacts in Thor's&nbsp;
collection is the one he's best known for:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:39.680
His iconic hammer, Mjolnir. While it's best known&nbsp;
for its ability to summon and control lightning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:43.760
the hammer's versatility is equally&nbsp;
impressive. Not to mention the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:48.560
that the Odinson is one of only a handful of&nbsp;
people who have been able to wield the weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:54.240
at all. Chances are, there's no Marvel&nbsp;
weapon out there with a higher price tag.

